      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum for amlodipine, and it could cause severe, possibly fatal, low blood pressure. I wouldn't enter this dose for anyone, including a physician, unless there were a documented clinical reason and a pharmacist had reviewed it.\n- **The order needs a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so the order has to come from a prescriber who is responsible for this patient's care.\n\n**What will get this done:**\n1. Have the patient's attending or covering physician on the medicine service review the request.\n2. If amlodipine is right for the patient, they can order a standard dose, likely 5 mg once daily, up to a maximum of 10 mg. I can enter that as soon as they give it to me.\n3. If anyone is unsure about the dose, the on-call pharmacist can help.\n\nIf this was a typo and the intended dose was 5 mg, ask the patient's prescriber to confirm it and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
